thing's really wrong. Right when I heard her voice, I just broke down into tears. I was tired of wasting my life away in a body I hated. Avoiding mirrors, not taking pictures, rarely getting a second look from anyone. Not hiding under baggy clothes even in the summer. She went quiet for a second and said, go to the cupboard on the hall. Take those little yellow droppers with the phytostrogens, and you won't have to worry at all. She said the women in Brazil with the curves everyone talks about and doing anything special with the diet. It's not about what you eat. Diet. It's about estrogen. Diet. The hormone that tells your body where to actually put weight, stress, genetics, years of it never firing right. All of that can throw it off, so your body just dumps everything in your belly instead of your hips, thighs, and booty. She said for generations. Oh, Brazilian women have used phytoestrogens, macaroon, fenugreek, ashwagandha to wake that signal back up and finally put the weight where it belongs. Once you fix that signal, everything finally falls into place. I trusted her. Took my first drop. Didn't feel much, but as the days went on, my appetite started gonna I got upset, but then she calmed down and grabbed my hand and said, how did you do it? I need to know I can't even be mad at you for stealing the show. I handed her a bottle of what my auntie told me to take. She texted me weeks later saying, girl, you are so right. I wish I knew about this before my wedding night. I filled out everywhere I wanted. My confidence, the way people look at me now, it's all different. I feel like a whole new person. It's not about trying harder. It's about giving your body the signal it needs. Brazilian women already figured this out. I ordered a few bottles for my sister and me because it's buy two get one free. And they even let you try it risk free with a ninety day\",\"callToAction\":\"SHOP NOW\",\"landingPageUrl\":\"https://shopamua.com/products/amua-vitaldrops\",\"landingPa